    # Operations runbook — Business Evidence Wallet
    
    Technically competent operator guide. No guessing. Do **not** paste secrets,
    invite codes, or customer evidence into chat.
    
    ## Current truth
    
    Current master: f44d55cad3c24cb49e8793a2cb348387d4c9ce19
    Release GO: no
    
    Local PostgreSQL 18 is the fully gated clean-room path. A DigitalOcean pilot
    origin is live (see [HOSTED.md](./HOSTED.md)). Neon/Vercel remains separately
    blocked until Andrew injects those credentials.
    
    ## DEPLOY (DigitalOcean pilot, when SSH authorised)
    
    1. Confirm the release-candidate SHA (PR #14 / `cursor/release-readiness-8a5b`
       atop `deployment/reconciled-pilot-20260914`). Do not deploy `master` without
       Andrew — `master` diverged and lacks this pilot's deploy/ops surface.
    2. On the droplet (`/opt/business-evidence-wallet`): fetch, checkout the SHA,
       `npm ci`, `npm run build`, restart `evidence-wallet.service` (unit in
       `deploy/digitalocean/`). Nginx TLS config is in
       `deploy/digitalocean/evidence-wallet.nginx`.
    3. Confirm host env includes `BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://46-101-16-174.sslip.io`
       (required by `startup-production.sh`). The script defaults
       `WALLET_SIGNUP_OPEN=false` and `CHAPELGATE_MCP_SETUP_UI=false` when unset —
       required production control for the DO pilot (MCP credential mint stays
       closed; MCP Bearer remains host-level privilege — see CONTROL_MCP.md).
       Optional overrides: `/etc/evidence-wallet.env` via systemd EnvironmentFile —
       do **not** set `CHAPELGATE_MCP_SETUP_UI=true` on the public pilot.
    4. `HOSTED_ORIGIN=https://46-101-16-174.sslip.io npm run test:hosted-probe`
       Expect `/ready` with `signupOpen: false` and (after this RC) `mcpSetupUi: false`.
    5. Record the deployed SHA. Do not claim the live origin matches a candidate
       until this step is done.
    
    ## DEPLOY (Vercel/Neon, when authorised)
    
    1. Confirm the git SHA of the release-candidate branch. Do not deploy `master`
       without Andrew.
    2. Confirm Vercel production branch is the RC branch. Deployment Protection **on**.
    3. Inject (never commit): pooled TLS `DATABASE_URL`, `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` (≥32 random bytes), `BETTER_AUTH_URL` = exact `https://` origin, `WALLET_SIGNUP_OPEN=false`.
    4. Run `node scripts/staging-preflight.mjs --hosted` in an environment that has those vars. Expect `ok: true`. The script never prints secrets.
    5. Deploy the RC SHA. `npm run build` applies every pending file in `migrations/` (including `0027_v2_gateway_phase_o.sql`).
    6. `HOSTED_ORIGIN=https://<origin> node scripts/hosted-probe.mjs`
    7. `HOSTED_ORIGIN=https://<origin> node scripts/hosted-acceptance.mjs`  
       If the result is `deployment-protection`, leave protection on and supply a signed-in operator session. Do not disable it to make the test pass.
    
    ## VERIFY
    
    Local:
    
    ```text
    npm run check:auth
    npm run typecheck
    npm run lint
    npm test
    npm run test:app
    npm run test:concurrency-pg
    npm run test:persistence
    npm run test:http-persistence
    npm run test:backup
    npm run test:live-idor
    node scripts/mutation-isolation.mjs
    node scripts/e2e-demo.mjs
    npm run test:secret-scan
    node scripts/staging-preflight.mjs
    DATABASE_URL=$(node scripts/pg-local.mjs url) npm run build
    ```
    
    Hosted: `GET /health` → `{"ok":true,"db":"up"}`. `GET /ready` → `authOrigin: true`, `signupOpen: false`. Then the synthetic operator journey on throwaway data only.
    
    ## ROLL BACK
    
    Local: stop the app, restore the last physical backup (`pg-backup.mjs restore <tar> --replace-live-data`), check out the previous SHA, start Postgres + migrate + app, confirm `/health` and a sign-in.
    
    Hosted: redeploy the previous candidate SHA. Use Neon PITR if data must move back. Do **not** disable TLS, auth, tenant checks, or signup closure.
    
    ## DATABASE BACKUP
    
    Local: `npm run test:backup` proves the isolated path. Operator backup: `node scripts/pg-backup.mjs backup`. Archives are not customer exports.
    
    Hosted: configure Neon PITR / backups on the Neon side. Application tar backup is for the local cluster only.
    
    ## DATABASE RESTORE
    
    `node scripts/pg-backup.mjs restore <archive.tar.gz> --replace-live-data`  
    Without the flag the CLI exits 2 (will not overwrite live `data/postgres`). Prove on the isolated port first.
    
    ## FAILED MIGRATION
    
    `scripts/migrate.mjs` applies each file in one transaction and records `_migrations`. A failed file rolls back; retry is safe. Do not edit an already-applied file — add a new `00xx_*.sql`. If 0009/0010 archive orphan facts, that is intentional (dangling/cross-org sources cannot stay GREEN). They do not delete fact rows.
    
    ## AUTH FAILURE
    
    - LAN IP over HTTP will not keep `__Host-` cookies. Use `localhost` or HTTPS.
    - Hosted sessions bounce: `BETTER_AUTH_URL` does not match the browser origin.
    - `/ready` `"authOrigin": false`: HTTPS origin missing.
    - Rotate `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` only with a planned sign-out of every session.
    
    ## DATABASE OUTAGE
    
    Symptoms: `/health` 503, UI “Database unavailable”, scrubbed `[db] pool error` logs.
    
    1. Local: `node scripts/pg-local.mjs status` then `start` then `npm run db:migrate`.
    2. Hosted: check Neon status. Do not set `sslmode=disable`.
    3. Confirm `/health` 200 before sending operators back.
    
    ## COMPROMISED SECRET
    
    1. Rotate the affected secret (`BETTER_AUTH_SECRET`, `DATABASE_URL` password, `XAI_API_KEY`, invite codes).
    2. Do not commit the new value. Do not paste it into chat.
    3. Re-invite members (old invite ids die). Audit for unexpected memberships.
    4. Record the incident; do not claim the leak never happened.
    
    ## TENANT-ISOLATION INCIDENT
    
    1. Do not relax tests.
    2. `npm run test:live-idor` against the running app.
    3. `node scripts/mutation-isolation.mjs`
    4. If confirmed: take the origin off the network, preserve logs, notify Andrew.
    
